  "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*",
